{
  "comment": "Plugin-panel pattern (mopho/esq1). Rows follow the Matrix-6/1000 voice: DCO 1/2 -> mix -> VCF (+ DCO 1 -> VCF FM) -> VCA 1 -> VCA 2 (Env 2), then the hard-wired modulators (Env 1 -> VCF, Env 2 -> VCA 2, Env 3 -> FM; LFO 1 -> both DCO freqs, LFO 2 -> both PWs, Ramp n -> LFO n amp), then the 10-slot matrix, tracking generator and portamento/keyboard. The Matrix-1000 has no panel editing, so every control here is editor-only. DCO uses one select (select.shared 'dco'); the two LFO groups share 'lfo' (LFO n's ramp is Ramp n; 'spd mod' is pressure for LFO 1, keyboard for LFO 2); envelopes share 'env' and their 'dest amt' cell resolves to the env's hard-wired amount (vcfEnv1 / vca2Env2 / vcfFmEnv3). 'levers' edits the fixed bend / vibrato / portamento / key-track switches of DCO 1, DCO 2 or the VCF (DCO 1 has no key-track switch). The mod matrix slot select picks one of 10 slots; a source or destination of 'none' empties the slot (the driver writes 0/0 to both).",
